From: PlasmaDrifter <118319137+PlasmaDrifter@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 19:05:12 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/4] fix(wayland): auto-switch to XCB backend under Wayland to
 allow LibVLC embedding

LibVLC 3.0 does not support embedding video into native Wayland surfaces via
libvlc_media_player_set_xwindow(), causing video to detach and pop up in a
separate floating window.

When running inside a Wayland session without an explicit QT_QPA_PLATFORM set,
automatically configure QT_QPA_PLATFORM=xcb before QApplication initialization
so that Kaffeine runs under XWayland and embeds video cleanly.
---
 src/main.cpp | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/main.cpp b/src/main.cpp
index d13dfc7..b50924b 100644
--- a/src/main.cpp
+++ b/src/main.cpp
@@ -207,6 +207,12 @@ KaffeineApplication::~KaffeineApplication()
 
 int main(int argc, char *argv[])
 {
+	// Wayland fix: LibVLC cannot embed video into native Wayland surfaces.
+	// Force the X11 (xcb) platform backend under Wayland so LibVLC embeds video into the Kaffeine window.
+	if (qEnvironmentVariableIsEmpty("QT_QPA_PLATFORM") && qEnvironmentVariableIsSet("WAYLAND_DISPLAY")) {
+		qputenv("QT_QPA_PLATFORM", "xcb");
+	}
+
 	qInstallMessageHandler(verboseMessageHandler);
 
 	KLocalizedString::setApplicationDomain("kaffeine");
